cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SiliconBench, please cite it as below."
title: "SiliconBench: A PPA-Aware Benchmark for LLM and Agent RTL Design"
abstract: >-
  SiliconBench is a power-, performance-, and area-aware benchmark for evaluating
  large language models and agents on register-transfer-level hardware design. It
  scores generated and agent-repaired RTL through a pinned open-source synthesis
  and static-timing flow, treating functional correctness as a severability gate
  and PPA as the primary score relative to a human-reviewed reference.
type: software
